From: Surface bringup contributors <surface-bringup@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel-edp: recognize LGD 0x07ad panel

The Surface Laptop for Business 13in 1st Ed with Snapdragon reports the
LGD 0x07ad panel identity. Recognize it so panel-edp uses the measured
panel timing delays instead of the generic conservative fallback.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-edp.c
@@ -2138,5 +2138,6 @@ static const struct edp_panel_entry edp_panels[] = {
	 EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x06b2, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "LP129WT232166"),
	 EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x0778, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "134WT1"),
+	EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x07ad, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "LP130WU112423"),
	 EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('L', 'G', 'D', 0x07fe, &delay_200_500_e200_d200, "LP116WHA-SPB1"),

	 EDP_PANEL_ENTRY('S', 'H', 'P', 0x1511, &delay_200_500_e50, "LQ140M1JW48"),
-- 
2.43.0
